Design: We introduce focal loss (gamma=2, alpha=0.25) in place of the standard BCEWithLogitsLoss to focus the model on harder examples and improve generalization without altering the fairness-driven sampler. All other components (DenseNet‐121 backbone, weighted sampler for skin tones, data splits, augmentations, and prediction pipeline) remain unchanged. We then train for 5 epochs, track the best validation AUROC, save the best model, and produce a submission.csv with malignancy probabilities for all images.
