Design: I propose integrating a OneCycleLR scheduler during training to cyclically vary the learning rate between a low start value and a higher peak (e.g., max_lr=1e-3), which often improves convergence and generalization. We keep the existing weighted sampling by skin tone, FocalLoss, DenseNet-121 backbone, and 4-way flip TTA unchanged. We initialize OneCycleLR based on the number of epochs and training steps, call scheduler.step() after each optimizer.step(), and then measure validation AUROC as before. This atomic change should yield a small but meaningful boost in test‐time performance without compromising fairness.
